List is a pre-defined interface in java.util package introduced from JDK 1.2. There are a number of classes that implements the list interface.
i) ArrayList : The underlined data structure of ArrayList is Resizable/Growable array. 
ii) LinkedList : The underlined data structure of LinkedList is Doubly linked list.
iii) Vector : The underlined data structure of Vector is Resizable/Growable array. 
iv) Stack : The underlined data structure of Stack is Resizable/Growable array. 

Specifications of List collections:
> It is index based. 
> It is of dynamic size. 
> It maintains the insertion order.
> Duplicate and null values are allowed.
